{"id":"benefit-cost-by-department","title":"The cost of a job beyond pay, by department","tier":"REDFLAG","question":"Which departments carry the highest benefit cost against salary and for each person, and how far apart are they?","finding":"Among 42 departments with 50 or more people paid in fiscal 2026, benefits run from 30.2% of regular salary in City Attorney to 56.8% in Sheriff, followed by Adult Probation (49.1%) and Juvenile Probation (47.4%). For each person the highest is Sheriff at $72,164. The spread comes mostly from the retirement column: 38.3% of salary at the top against 10.9% at the bottom.","how":"City payroll file, fiscal 2026 with fiscal 2013 for comparison; the same columns as the year-by-year table, by department. Departments with fewer than 50 people paid are left out. Ranked by benefits as a share of regular salary.","limits":"Departments differ for structural reasons. Police, fire and sheriff’s staff belong to separate “safety” retirement plans under the City Charter, which the pension fund’s valuation reports apart from other staff, and the City’s payment differs by plan. A department with many low-paid or part-time staff shows health cover as a large share of a small salary. A department with many temporary staff may show a low retirement share. None of this is a choice made by the department.","columns":[{"k":"department","t":"Department","type":"text"},{"k":"people","t":"People paid, fiscal 2026","type":"int"},{"k":"benefits","t":"All benefits","type":"usd"},{"k":"perPerson","t":"Per person","type":"usd"},{"k":"share","t":"Share of regular salary","type":"pct"},{"k":"retirementShare","t":"Retirement","type":"pct"},{"k":"healthShare","t":"Health and dental","type":"pct"},{"k":"otherShare","t":"Other benefits","type":"pct"},{"k":"shareFirst","t":"Share of salary, fiscal 2013","type":"pct"},{"k":"perPersonFirst","t":"Per person, fiscal 2013","type":"usd"}],"rows":[{"department":"Sheriff","people":1067,"benefits":76999465,"perPerson":72164,"